WEBVTT

1
00:01:19.875 --> 00:01:22.041
On the battlefield of Kurukshetra,

2
00:01:22.041 --> 00:01:23.833
when Arjun had to make,

3
00:01:23.833 --> 00:01:26.291
the decision between life and dharma,

4
00:01:26.291 --> 00:01:28.583
he sought guidance from his
charioteer, Lord Krishna.

5
00:01:28.583 --> 00:01:30.750
He sought guidance.

6
00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:32.666
The teachings Lord Krishna gave

7
00:01:32.666 --> 00:01:35.458
were not merely an inspiration for war.

8
00:01:35.458 --> 00:01:38.333
They were a complete philosophy of life.

9
00:01:38.333 --> 00:01:40.708
When Arjun heard those words,

10
00:01:40.708 --> 00:01:44.708
the fog of doubt settled within him began to lift.

11
00:01:44.708 --> 00:01:47.125
The darkness of confusion faded.

12
00:01:47.125 --> 00:01:48.750
Now he knew,

13
00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.166
this is no ordinary friend.

14
00:01:51.166 --> 00:01:54.541
This is Parabrahma Himself, the Supreme Lord,

15
00:01:54.541 --> 00:01:59.000
who pervades all of creation
and is the foundation of all.

16
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:03.000
But Arjun's curiosity was not yet complete.

17
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.375
Now he wished to behold

18
00:02:04.375 --> 00:02:06.500
that Viraat Rupa,

19
00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.041
in which all the creations

20
00:02:08.041 --> 00:02:10.208
of the universe are contained.

21
00:02:10.208 --> 00:02:14.166
A form that is infinite, boundless,
and which, on beholding,

22
00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:16.000
not only awakens reverence,

23
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.583
but also establishes the truth.

24
00:02:18.583 --> 00:02:21.791
Arjun folded his hands and prayed,

25
00:02:21.791 --> 00:02:23.125
'O Lord,

26
00:02:23.125 --> 00:02:25.000
if You are pleased,

27
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.541
show me that divine form,

28
00:02:27.541 --> 00:02:31.375
so that I may experience Your supreme nature.'

29
00:02:31.375 --> 00:02:35.625
This prayer was not merely to
satisfy his own curiosity.

30
00:02:35.625 --> 00:02:37.375
Arjun's purpose was

31
00:02:37.375 --> 00:02:39.958
that the world too should
come to know this truth –

32
00:02:39.958 --> 00:02:42.708
who is the true Lord?

33
00:02:42.708 --> 00:02:45.875
So that in the future, when any false person

34
00:02:45.875 --> 00:02:47.916
claims to be God,

35
00:02:47.916 --> 00:02:51.250
people may not be trapped in that lie.

36
00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:52.375
Lord Krishna's divine play

37
00:02:52.375 --> 00:02:54.958
was not only for Arjun.

38
00:02:54.958 --> 00:02:57.458
It was meant to guide humanity

39
00:02:57.458 --> 00:02:59.958
for ages to come.

40
00:03:04.791 --> 00:03:08.250
Arjun, expressing gratitude to Lord Krishna,

41
00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:10.250
begins his words,

42
00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:13.166
that He has removed his doubts.

43
00:03:13.166 --> 00:03:14.750
He acknowledges

44
00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.083
that through Lord Krishna's grace,

45
00:03:16.083 --> 00:03:19.708
he has received deep spiritual knowledge,

46
00:03:19.708 --> 00:03:23.666
and now he understands the
nature of existence,

47
00:03:23.666 --> 00:03:24.833
which is –

48
00:03:24.833 --> 00:03:27.208
how all beings arise

49
00:03:27.208 --> 00:03:29.916
and then pass away.

50
00:03:29.916 --> 00:03:32.375
But even after accepting Lord Krishna's words

51
00:03:32.375 --> 00:03:34.041
as truth,

52
00:03:34.041 --> 00:03:36.500
Arjun wishes to see for himself

53
00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:38.666
Lord Krishna's divine presence

54
00:03:38.666 --> 00:03:41.833
spread across all creation,
although Lord Krishna,

55
00:03:41.833 --> 00:03:46.000
in Chapter 10, has already
described His vibhutis.

56
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.125
Arjun desires a direct experience

57
00:03:48.125 --> 00:03:51.833
of Lord Krishna's all-pervading cosmic form.

58
00:03:51.833 --> 00:03:53.750
This desire is not because

59
00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:56.750
he doubts Lord Krishna's words,

60
00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:59.000
but he wishes to gain

61
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.166
deeper knowledge of it,

62
00:04:01.166 --> 00:04:03.500
and he also wants to reveal

63
00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:07.916
Lord Krishna's incomparable
supremacy to all others.

64
00:04:07.916 --> 00:04:08.708
Arjun

65
00:04:08.708 --> 00:04:12.208
makes this prayer with deep humility.

66
00:04:12.208 --> 00:04:14.833
He does not stubbornly demand

67
00:04:14.833 --> 00:04:18.291
that Lord Krishna show His Viraat Rupa,

68
00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:20.625
but humbly requests,

69
00:04:20.625 --> 00:04:23.875
'If You think I am worthy,

70
00:04:23.875 --> 00:04:26.875
please show me this form.'

71
00:04:26.875 --> 00:04:29.541
This request reflects an essential principle

72
00:04:29.541 --> 00:04:32.625
of the spiritual life –

73
00:04:32.625 --> 00:04:35.458
the Lord is not compelled, merely
by someone's curiosity

74
00:04:35.458 --> 00:04:39.666
or effort, to reveal Himself.

75
00:04:39.666 --> 00:04:41.333
Rather, His divine vision

76
00:04:41.333 --> 00:04:44.416
comes only through His grace.

77
00:04:44.416 --> 00:04:46.083
Arjun acknowledges

78
00:04:46.083 --> 00:04:49.666
that Lord Krishna alone is Yogeshvara,

79
00:04:49.666 --> 00:04:52.500
the master of all mystical powers.

80
00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:54.541
In this form, He has the ability

81
00:04:54.541 --> 00:04:57.458
to show an infinite vision.

82
00:04:57.458 --> 00:05:00.333
This moment is significant because from here

83
00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:04.208
a new direction becomes visible
in the Bhagavad Gita.

84
00:05:04.208 --> 00:05:06.708
Instead of understanding divine reality

85
00:05:06.708 --> 00:05:08.458
only through intellect,

86
00:05:08.458 --> 00:05:10.125
moving toward seeing

87
00:05:10.125 --> 00:05:12.708
and directly experiencing it.

88
00:05:12.708 --> 00:05:14.666
Until this point, Lord Krishna's teachings

89
00:05:14.666 --> 00:05:16.416
have been centred on knowledge, devotion,

90
00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:20.125
and understanding of His divine position.

91
00:05:20.125 --> 00:05:21.958
Now Lord Krishna is about to give Arjun

92
00:05:21.958 --> 00:05:25.750
a direct vision of His cosmic presence.

93
00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:28.375
A form that even great saints

94
00:05:28.375 --> 00:05:31.958
and devas have rarely beheld.

95
00:05:31.958 --> 00:05:33.416
Arjun's humility

96
00:05:33.416 --> 00:05:36.208
gives a lesson for the path of devotion –

97
00:05:36.208 --> 00:05:40.333
that true seekers do not demand
spiritual experiences,

98
00:05:40.333 --> 00:05:43.500
but, surrendered to the divine will,

99
00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:45.000
for that will to be fulfilled,

100
00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:48.458
they pray from the depths of their heart.

101
00:05:48.458 --> 00:05:50.958
This distinction between humble surrender

102
00:05:50.958 --> 00:05:54.666
and arrogant expectation is important.

103
00:05:54.666 --> 00:05:58.583
Just as a servant, rather than
claiming authority,

104
00:05:58.583 --> 00:06:02.041
patiently awaits the master's permission,

105
00:06:02.041 --> 00:06:03.000
in the same way Arjun

106
00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:07.250
surrenders himself to Lord Krishna's will.

107
00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:10.458
For all sincere spiritual seekers,

108
00:06:10.458 --> 00:06:13.375
he sets an example.

109
00:06:13.375 --> 00:06:15.041
Thus this conversation

110
00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:17.166
moves toward one of the Bhagavad Gita's

111
00:06:17.166 --> 00:06:19.750
most thrilling revelations unfolding.

112
00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:21.500
One of them is

113
00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:24.958
the magnificent display of the
Viraat Rupa, which

114
00:06:24.958 --> 00:06:27.166
will further strengthen the power

115
00:06:27.166 --> 00:06:31.000
and glory of Lord Krishna's divine nature.

116
00:06:35.791 --> 00:06:40.083
When you wish to learn
something from someone,

117
00:06:40.083 --> 00:06:44.666
what is the attitude of your mind?

118
00:06:44.666 --> 00:06:47.291
To learn with humility,

119
00:06:47.291 --> 00:06:50.875
or to receive knowledge with
a sense of entitlement?

120
00:06:50.875 --> 00:06:55.333
When you seek spiritual knowledge,

121
00:06:55.333 --> 00:06:58.916
do so with humility.

122
00:06:58.916 --> 00:07:00.250
Not as a challenge

123
00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:04.291
to prove or to test.

124
00:07:04.291 --> 00:07:05.875
Arjun

125
00:07:05.875 --> 00:07:09.083
understood this well.

126
00:07:09.083 --> 00:07:11.000
Even after hearing My words

127
00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:14.875
and understanding My divine nature,

128
00:07:14.875 --> 00:07:18.083
he prayed with respect and trust

129
00:07:18.083 --> 00:07:22.458
to behold My Viraat Rupa.

130
00:07:22.458 --> 00:07:26.750
He did not demand proof, but said,

131
00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:29.333
'If You think

132
00:07:29.333 --> 00:07:31.458
I am worthy,

133
00:07:31.458 --> 00:07:35.708
please show me this.'

134
00:07:35.708 --> 00:07:37.958
This humble approach

135
00:07:37.958 --> 00:07:40.666
opened the door to a deeper experience.

136
00:07:40.666 --> 00:07:45.166
In life, whether you are learning spiritual truth

137
00:07:45.166 --> 00:07:47.791
or acquiring a skill,

138
00:07:47.791 --> 00:07:52.916
humility helps you move forward.

139
00:07:52.916 --> 00:07:58.041
When you think you know everything,

140
00:07:58.041 --> 00:08:00.916
then learning stops.

141
00:08:00.916 --> 00:08:05.750
But when you come with an open heart,

142
00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:07.791
you receive far more

143
00:08:07.791 --> 00:08:10.916
knowledge than expected.

144
00:08:10.916 --> 00:08:15.791
A stream flows from above to below.
To receive the water, humbly bowing,

145
00:08:15.791 --> 00:08:18.958
you must place the pot beneath the flow.

146
00:08:18.958 --> 00:08:23.125
If you show pride and hold the pot above,

147
00:08:23.125 --> 00:08:26.791
then tell me, will water enter that pot?

148
00:08:26.791 --> 00:08:28.708
Never.

149
00:08:28.708 --> 00:08:31.541
In this example, the stream is

150
00:08:31.541 --> 00:08:35.166
the knowledge coming from the teacher,
and the pot is

151
00:08:35.166 --> 00:08:37.500
your heart.

152
00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:40.500
So to receive knowledge from the teacher, 

153
00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:43.708
you must bow before them.

154
00:08:43.708 --> 00:08:46.708
Humility allows you to listen, to understand,

155
00:08:46.708 --> 00:08:48.625
and to receive knowledge

156
00:08:48.625 --> 00:08:51.500
with gratitude.

157
00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:53.541
Remember,

158
00:08:53.541 --> 00:08:57.416
true knowledge is a gift.

159
00:08:57.416 --> 00:09:01.250
Not a prize to be won.

160
00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:06.583
When you seek it with respect and patience,

161
00:09:06.583 --> 00:09:13.250
then I guide you toward those truths

162
00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:17.458
that transform your entire life.

163
00:09:22.375 --> 00:09:23.875
A family

164
00:09:23.875 --> 00:09:29.250
grows strong only through mutual support.

165
00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:31.500
When someone asks you

166
00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:35.000
for the help of your experience,

167
00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:38.875
do you genuinely assist them,

168
00:09:38.875 --> 00:09:41.541
or do you begin scolding them

169
00:09:41.541 --> 00:09:45.833
for their flaws?

170
00:09:45.833 --> 00:09:47.708
In family life,

171
00:09:47.708 --> 00:09:51.166
seeking guidance with humility

172
00:09:51.166 --> 00:09:54.208
strengthens relationships

173
00:09:54.208 --> 00:09:56.791
and opens the door to understanding.

174
00:09:56.791 --> 00:09:58.625
Just as Arjun,

175
00:09:58.625 --> 00:10:01.666
not to test My greatness,

176
00:10:01.666 --> 00:10:04.583
but to gain clarity,

177
00:10:04.583 --> 00:10:08.541
requested Me with respect,

178
00:10:08.541 --> 00:10:09.083
in the same way

179
00:10:09.083 --> 00:10:13.500
you too should approach
your elder family members

180
00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:15.958
with this same spirit.

181
00:10:15.958 --> 00:10:20.875
When you ask for help without ego,

182
00:10:20.875 --> 00:10:25.833
you receive genuine support and knowledge.

183
00:10:25.833 --> 00:10:27.166
In the same way,

184
00:10:27.166 --> 00:10:30.750
when you guide others,

185
00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:35.000
whether they are your children, siblings,

186
00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:36.625
or spouse,

187
00:10:36.625 --> 00:10:39.500
do it with kindness,

188
00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:43.708
not to show your own superiority.

189
00:10:43.708 --> 00:10:46.666
The children at home may not have scored

190
00:10:46.666 --> 00:10:49.666
well in an exam.

191
00:10:49.666 --> 00:10:52.166
Their mind, instead of studying,

192
00:10:52.166 --> 00:10:54.625
may be drifting toward mobile games,

193
00:10:54.625 --> 00:10:57.666
and they themselves, troubled by this,

194
00:10:57.666 --> 00:11:00.375
come to you asking for guidance.

195
00:11:00.375 --> 00:11:02.583
Then, without getting angry,

196
00:11:02.583 --> 00:11:05.875
explain to them lovingly

197
00:11:05.875 --> 00:11:09.708
and share the benefit of your experience.

198
00:11:09.708 --> 00:11:12.000
Inspire them to move forward.

199
00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:14.375
Do not make them feel small.

200
00:11:14.375 --> 00:11:16.833
I showed Arjun My Viraat Rupa,

201
00:11:16.833 --> 00:11:20.125
not to prove My power,

202
00:11:20.125 --> 00:11:23.333
but to help dissolve his confusion

203
00:11:23.333 --> 00:11:27.166
and show him the truth.

204
00:11:27.166 --> 00:11:30.875
In the same way, when you give advice,

205
00:11:30.875 --> 00:11:33.833
offer it not to control,

206
00:11:33.833 --> 00:11:38.458
but with the intention of helping.

207
00:11:38.458 --> 00:11:41.208
True guidance

208
00:11:41.208 --> 00:11:44.291
comes from a spirit of care,

209
00:11:44.291 --> 00:11:46.041
not from ego.

210
00:11:46.041 --> 00:11:49.166
And when family members experience

211
00:11:49.166 --> 00:11:52.791
that their flaws are not being sought out, but

212
00:11:52.791 --> 00:11:55.250
that they are being supported,

213
00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:58.291
then, receiving this support,
they begin to trust you

214
00:11:58.291 --> 00:12:01.166
even more.

215
00:12:01.166 --> 00:12:03.125
This spirit of asking humbly

216
00:12:03.125 --> 00:12:06.708
and teaching with a warm heart

217
00:12:06.708 --> 00:12:09.791
fills your home with respect,

218
00:12:09.791 --> 00:12:12.625
love, and understanding.

219
00:12:17.375 --> 00:12:20.666
When a new employee comes to an office,

220
00:12:20.666 --> 00:12:24.041
instead of learning how things work here,

221
00:12:24.041 --> 00:12:27.791
they remain proud of their past experience.

222
00:12:27.791 --> 00:12:31.000
Will they last there?

223
00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:33.208
Never. Not at all.

224
00:12:33.208 --> 00:12:35.625
Because no matter how
much experience one has,

225
00:12:35.625 --> 00:12:40.125
there is always something more to learn,

226
00:12:40.125 --> 00:12:42.000
and the work of learning

227
00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:45.583
simply cannot happen with arrogance.

228
00:12:45.583 --> 00:12:50.000
In professional life, the right
approach to learning

229
00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:55.791
is a blend of curiosity and humility.

230
00:12:55.791 --> 00:12:57.666
When I said

231
00:12:57.666 --> 00:13:03.291
that with just a fraction of My energy

232
00:13:03.291 --> 00:13:06.208
I pervade all of creation,

233
00:13:06.208 --> 00:13:09.875
Arjun did not challenge Me,

234
00:13:09.875 --> 00:13:10.708
but

235
00:13:10.708 --> 00:13:14.708
he did not accept it blindly either.

236
00:13:14.708 --> 00:13:19.291
Instead, with respect and openness,

237
00:13:19.291 --> 00:13:23.416
he prayed to behold My Viraat Rupa.

238
00:13:23.416 --> 00:13:26.541
He also said that only if

239
00:13:26.541 --> 00:13:29.875
I considered him worthy of
beholding this Vishwaroop –

240
00:13:29.875 --> 00:13:33.208
the Universal Form – should I accept

241
00:13:33.208 --> 00:13:36.291
his prayer.

242
00:13:36.291 --> 00:13:38.250
This approach of staying clear

243
00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:40.583
without ego

244
00:13:40.583 --> 00:13:44.000
opens the path to real growth.

245
00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:47.458
In your career, asking questions

246
00:13:47.458 --> 00:13:48.666
and gaining deeper

247
00:13:48.666 --> 00:13:51.791
understanding is important, but always

248
00:13:51.791 --> 00:13:54.416
with respect for those

249
00:13:54.416 --> 00:13:59.125
who have more experience than you.

250
00:13:59.125 --> 00:14:01.500
Curiosity drives new approaches

251
00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:05.458
and progress, while humility

252
00:14:05.458 --> 00:14:08.041
keeps you eager to learn

253
00:14:08.041 --> 00:14:09.750
from others.

254
00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:13.041
When you ask questions honestly,

255
00:14:13.041 --> 00:14:16.041
not to prove someone wrong,

256
00:14:16.041 --> 00:14:18.500
but to gain knowledge,

257
00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:21.833
then people are always ready to guide

258
00:14:21.833 --> 00:14:26.458
and support you.

259
00:14:26.458 --> 00:14:28.708
When you engage with your work

260
00:14:28.708 --> 00:14:32.208
and relationships with this mindset,

261
00:14:32.208 --> 00:14:33.958
then you will receive both knowledge

262
00:14:33.958 --> 00:14:37.208
and the respect of those around you,

263
00:14:37.208 --> 00:14:39.083
both,

264
00:14:39.083 --> 00:14:42.083
which will open the path to lasting success.
